lk9=d7,lk_=[0,bl,[0,i,bhP]],lk$=eU,lla=[0,cd,[0,i,eU]],llb="\nPlaces the **statics** refractor on the bindings at the given paths: a GUI type-ascription overlay (offside type cell) for human-readable types on expressions.\nThis does not change program text. If a runtime probe is on the same binding, it is replaced by statics (same transition as the editor\xe2\x80\x99s statics toggle).\nCollapsed definitions are auto-expanded when statics are placed so overlays are visible.\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings\n\nSee the system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** for how statics relate to probes and livelits.\n",llc=[0,[0,ln,[0,R,[0,[0,cd,[0,i,jV]],[0,[0,kn,[0,R,[0,[0,lV,[0,R,[0,qgl,qgk]]],0]]],[0,[0,hX,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lV],0]]],0]]]]],0],lld=d7,lle=[0,bl,[0,i,bi_]],llf=eU,llg=[0,cd,[0,i,eU]],llh="\nRemoves **only** the statics refractor from the bindings at the given paths.\nRuntime probes on the same binding are left unchanged (unlike remove_probe).\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to clear statics overlays from\n",lli=[0,[0,ln,[0,R,[0,[0,cd,[0,i,jV]],[0,[0,kn,[0,R,[0,[0,lV,[0,R,[0,qgn,qgm]]],0]]],[0,[0,hX,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lV],0]]],0]]]]],0],llj=d7,llk=[0,bl,[0,i,bo$]],lll=eU,llm=[0,cd,[0,i,eU]],lln="\nToggles the statics refractor on or off for the bindings at the given paths (same behavior as the editor statics toggle).\nCollapsed definitions are auto-expanded when statics end up enabled.\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to toggle\n",llo=[0,[0,ln,[0,R,[0,[0,cd,[0,i,jV]],[0,[0,kn,[0,R,[0,[0,lV,[0,R,[0,qgp,qgo]]],0]]],[0,[0,hX,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lV],0]]],0]]]]],0],llp=d7,llq=[0,bl,[0,i,blv]],llr=eU,lls=[0,cd,[0,i,eU]],llt=[0,0,0],llD=[0,1],llC=I,llB=I,llA=I,llz=o,lly=cL,llx="Printer.add_indent: Not_found",llE=dl9,llF=[0,o],llG=[0,iH],llI=[0,"- **checkbox** \xe2\x80\x94 Toggle UI for boolean literals."],llJ=[0,"- **slider** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (integer)."],llK=[0,"- **sliderf** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (floating-point)."],llL=[0,"- **card** \xe2\x80\x94 **Playing-card** editor: a tuple `(Suit, Rank)` such as `(Hearts, Ace)` or a list of those tuples. **Not** for records, modules, or `{ let \xe2\x80\xa6; \xe2\x80\xa6 }` blocks."],llM=[0,'- **livelit** \xe2\x80\x94 Shows a livelit\'s GUI at a use `^name(model)`. Programs can DEFINE their own livelits \xe2\x80\x94 `let ^name = { type Model; type Action; type Expansion; init; update; view; expand } in ...` \xe2\x80\x94 giving any data type an embedded editing widget; write uses as `^^livelit(^name(model))`. Call `read_docs("livelits")` before defining one.'],llN=[0,"- **text** \xe2\x80\x94 Multiline string literal editor."],llO=[0,"- **table** \xe2\x80\x94 Spreadsheet-style editor for a **list of labeled tuples** sharing the same labels; the labels become column headers. Attaches off the **elaborated** form, so it can apply where the surface syntax alone is not yet a table."],llP=[0,"- **csv** \xe2\x80\x94 CSV **file import** UI. Attaches only when the definition is the **empty list** `[]`; after placement, import fills it with row/tuple syntax. Non-empty lists (e.g. `[1, 2, 3]`) **cannot** take this projector."],llQ=[0,'- **html** \xe2\x80\x94 Renders an HTML-valued expression live. An `(init, update, view, subs)` tuple runs as an interactive **app** the user can operate in place; make the app tuple the program\'s final expression, written as `^^html((init, update, view, subs))`. Call `read_docs("mvu")` before building one.'],llR=[0,"- **keybinding** \xe2\x80\x94 Key-capture editor for a string literal holding a keyboard shortcut; records the next chord pressed and commits it as the literal."],llS=[0,"- **color** \xe2\x80\x94 Colour picker for an `Oklch(l, c, h)` literal: a swatch plus lightness, chroma and hue sliders. Attaches only to that constructor applied to three float literals."],llT=[0,0,0],llU=[0,o,[0,"These are alternative UIs for literals and structured values that may already appear in code.",0]],llV=[0,"### Livelits (menu projectors)",0],llX=[0,o,0],llY=[0,o,[0,"### Syntax projector tools (Filbert)",[0,"`place_syntax_projector(kind, paths)`, `remove_syntax_projector(paths)`, and `toggle_syntax_projector(kind, paths)` apply **syntax projector** UIs to the term selected by each path.",[0,"`kind` must be a menu projector name (`fold`, `slider`, `sliderf`, `check`, `text`, `card`, `csv`, `table`, `livelit`) \xe2\x80\x94 not `probe` or `statics` (those use the probe/statics tools).",[0,o,[0,"**CRITICAL \xe2\x80\x94 livelits are not automatic:** Ordinary Hazel code (`let speed = 50`, `let is_active = true`, list literals, records) renders as **plain text** until you call **`place_syntax_projector`**.",[0,'If the user asks how livelits work, or wants sliders/checkboxes/CSV editors/text boxes, you **must** call `place_syntax_projector` with the right `kind` on each binding path (e.g. `slider` on `"speed"`, `check` on `"is_active"`, `text` on `"message"`, `csv` only when the RHS is `[]`, `card` only on playing-card tuples/lists\xe2\x80\x94see livelit lines above; nested paths like `"config/volume"`).',[0,"**Never** describe interactive widgets as present based only on `insert_*`, `update_*`, or other edit tools \xe2\x80\x94 that is false unless the matching `place_syntax_projector` calls succeeded.",[0,o,0]]]]]]]]],llZ=iy(["## Projectors and the agent view",o,"### Fold (`\xe2\x8b\xb1`)","A **fold** is a collapsed definition in the GUI: the definition shows as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (not source text).","Use `expand` / `collapse` (see **Paths** and **View Tools** above).",o,"### Runtime probe refractor","The **probe** refractor attaches to a binding and shows evaluated values in the agent view (e.g. `expr \xe2\x89\xa1 value`).","Tools: `place_probe`, `remove_probe`, `toggle_probe`.",o,"### Statics refractor (type overlay)","The **statics** refractor shows a type ascription overlay in the GUI (offside type cell) for human clarity.","It does not change program text; the agent\xe2\x80\x99s printed context may not mirror the overlay unless printing is extended.",o]),ll0=[0,"**Projectors**: **Folds** display as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (collapsed defs; expand/collapse in the full prompt).",[0,"**Refractors** overlay bindings: **probes** show runtime values (`\xe2\x89\xa1` in context); **statics** add a type overlay in the GUI.",[0,"**Livelits** are alternate UIs for literals (checkbox, slider/sliderf, text, card, csv, table, livelit, plus fold in the menu).",[0,"**Agent tools**: `place_syntax_projector` / `remove_syntax_projector` / `toggle_syntax_projector` (see full prompt).",[0,"Full detail lives in Filbert\xe2\x80\x99s live system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** section (this excerpt may be truncated).",0]]]]],ll6=[0,o],ll5="Editor.Meta.t_of_yojson",ll4="Editor.Meta.yojson_of_t",ll3="Editor.Meta.t_of_sexp",ll1="Editor.Meta.sexp_of_t",lmb=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],lma=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],lmc=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],ll$=[0,"Empty hole"],ll_=gr,ll9=[0,"Missing operator"],ll7=[0,0,1],ll8=[0,0,0],lmd=[0,[0,ln,[0,R,[0,[0,cd,[0,i,jV]],[0,[0,kn,[0,R,[0,[0,lV,[0,R,[0,qgr,qgq]]],0]]],[0,[0,hX,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lV],0]]],0]]]]],0],lme=d7,lmf=[0,bl,[0,i,bow]],lmg=eU,lmh=[0,cd,[0,i,eU]],lmi=[0,[0,ln,[0,R,[0,[0,cd,[0,i,jV]],[0,[0,kn,[0,R,[0,[0,lV,[0,R,[0,qgt,qgs]]],0]]],[0,[0,hX,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lV],0]]],0]]]]],0],lmj=d7,lmk=[0,bl,[0,i,blW]],lml=eU,lmm=[0,cd,[0,i,eU]],lmn=[0,[0,ln,[0,R,[0,[0,cd,[0,i,jV]],[0,[0,kn,[0,R,[0,[0,lV,[0,R,[0,qgv,qgu]]],0]]],[0,[0,hX,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lV],0]]],0]]]]],0],lmo=d7,lmp=[0,bl,[0,i,bkj]],lmq=eU,lmr=[0,cd,[0,i,eU]],lmH=[0,1],lmE=[0,MF],lmF=[0,I],lmG=cL,lmC=[0,40],lmB=[0,lq],lmD=o,lmA=[0,0],lmv=[0,1],lmw=[0,o],lmx=[0,iH],lmy=I,lmz=cL,lms=bm8,lmt=dKo,lmu=b17,lmI=[0,0],lmK=[0,fu,[0,qu,[0,em,0]]],lmN=[0,0],lmW=dnC,lmX="mod-root wrap did not yield a single module body",lmY="root sort is not fast-parseable (Exp and Mod only)",lmQ=[0,jb],lmR=[0,i0],lmS=i0,lmU=[0,aB],lmT=dh,lm